From: PS5_Proton
Subject: [PATCH] server: publish a bounded coherent retained-window snapshot

Keep authoritative window geometry, visibility, stacking, ownership and lifetime
in Wine. Add generation/native ownership to its private window-info response.
Publish a copied snapshot after window mutations and asynchronous destruction;
readers never walk Wine objects or acquire Wine's mutable-state lock. Preserve
request error state and use the same input desktop as hardware injection.
The first transport model marks shaped/layered rows unsupported explicitly.

--- a/server/protocol.def
+++ b/server/protocol.def
@@ -2705,6 +2705,8 @@
